# Serie D (EN): il Sole nei 12 segni, un discorso unico per segno che cita le tradizioni.
PLANET='Sun'
COVER_SUB='What your Sun feels like in each sign, drawing on Ptolemy, Barbault, Volguine, Blavatsky and Bailey.'
S=[
('Aries','Fire · cardinal','Exaltation','The Sun is exalted in Aries, and Ptolemy ties it to the equinox, where the days begin to grow longer than the nights. You feel that victory as a drive to start, to lead, to be first. Barbault and Volguine read Aries as the pure affirmation of the self: impulse before reflection, courage, speed, a temper that flares and cools fast. Bailey saw the soul taking its first step into form, a new cycle opened by a single act of will. The shadow is impatience and a need to win every argument. The lesson: let the fire build something.'),
('Taurus','Earth · fixed','Venus’s sign','Taurus is a fixed sign ruled by Venus, so the Sun stops rushing and takes root. You want what you can touch: good food, music, land, steady income, people who stay. Patience is a real strength here, and so is stubbornness; once you decide, you rarely turn back. The French school links Taurus with the body, the senses and endurance. Bailey called it the sign of light, where desire is slowly refined into understanding. The shadow is possessiveness and fear of change. The lesson: what you value should serve you, not own you.'),
('Gemini','Air · mutable','Mercury’s sign','Gemini is a double sign ruled by Mercury, and the Sun here is always two things at once: speaker and listener, student and teacher. You collect words, people and information, and you fit into any room. Barbault and Volguine place relationship and exchange at the heart of Gemini. Bailey saw its duality as the soul and the personality, both speaking and not yet sure which is which. The shadow is scattering and a restless mind that never lands. The lesson: depth comes from staying with one thing a little longer.'),
('Cancer','Water · cardinal','The Moon’s sign','Cancer is a tropical sign: the Sun turns at the summer solstice, and Ptolemy gives the sign to the Moon. The Sun here becomes receptive and protective. Your identity grows from home, family, memory and mood, and you sense what others need before they say it. An old tradition, kept by the Theosophists, called Cancer the gate through which souls enter life. Bailey saw a sign of mass life and of building a form to live in. The shadow is clinging and withdrawal. The lesson: a shell is for protection, not for hiding.'),
('Leo','Fire · fixed','The Sun’s own house','Ptolemy gives Leo to the Sun and Cancer to the Moon, the two lights. Here the Sun shines without effort. You are warm, proud and generous, with a need to create and to be seen. Barbault and Volguine read Leo as the creative self and natural authority. Blavatsky called the Sun the heart of the solar system, and Leo, the sign of the heart, carries that image. Bailey saw an individual finding full self-awareness, so that it can later serve the group. The shadow is vanity and a wound when ignored. The lesson: a true king lights the room for others.'),
('Virgo','Earth · mutable','Mercury’s sign','Virgo, ruled by Mercury, brings the Sun down to the field: harvest, craft, order, health. You see the detail others miss, and you show love by being useful. Barbault and Volguine stress analysis, service and discernment. Bailey took the old image of the Mother and the Child, spirit hidden in matter, and read the sign as the slow work of giving the ideal a real form. The shadow is perfectionism, worry and a harsh inner critic. The lesson: being useful does not require being flawless.'),
('Libra','Air · cardinal','Fall','Libra is the Sun’s fall, opposite its exaltation, and Ptolemy also calls it an equinoctial sign, where night begins to overtake day. The sign belongs to Venus and defines itself through others, so the Sun feels less sure of its own centre. You are fair, charming and a born diplomat. Barbault and Volguine read association and harmony; Bailey saw a balance between two forces and the mind that must choose between them. The shadow is indecision and pleasing everyone. The lesson: peace that costs you yourself is not peace.'),
('Scorpio','Water · fixed','Mars’s sign','Scorpio is a fixed water sign ruled by Mars, and the Sun goes below the surface. You feel strongly, show little and see through pretence. Crisis, secrets, desire and loss are your territory. The French school reads Scorpio as the sign of transformation; Bailey saw a sign of testing and initiation, where the warrior must cross his own illusions to be free. The shadow is jealousy, control and long memory for wounds. The lesson: every ending you survive teaches you how to begin again.'),
('Sagittarius','Fire · mutable','Jupiter’s sign','Sagittarius is ruled by Jupiter, and the Sun here looks to the horizon. You are frank, optimistic and hungry for freedom, travel, philosophy and meaning. You inspire others with sheer enthusiasm. Barbault and Volguine read expansion and a search for truth. Bailey saw the archer who aims straight at one goal, and when he reaches it, sees another beyond. The shadow is exaggeration, impatience with detail and preaching what you only just learned. The lesson: faith is stronger when it can tolerate a doubt.'),
('Capricorn','Earth · cardinal','Where the Sun turns','Capricorn is the winter solstice, where Ptolemy says the Sun turns and the light starts to return. It belongs to Saturn. You are patient, responsible and willing to work for years toward a goal, often serious young and lighter with age. An ancient tradition, taken up by Theosophy, called Capricorn the gate of the gods. Bailey saw the climb of the mountain goat, the will to manifest. Barbault and Volguine stress concentration and ambition. The shadow is coldness and fear of failing. The lesson: authority is stronger when it is human.'),
('Aquarius','Air · fixed','Opposite the Sun’s house','Aquarius is Saturn’s other house, directly opposite Leo, and the Sun feels slightly out of place. You are independent, inventive and committed to ideas bigger than yourself. Friends and causes matter more to you than applause. Modern astrologers in the French school add Uranus, the sign of emancipation and the unexpected. Bailey saw the water carrier, pouring out the water of life for others. The shadow is detachment and rebellion for its own sake. The lesson: belonging to a group does not mean dissolving in it.'),
('Pisces','Water · mutable','Jupiter’s sign','Pisces is a double water sign, given to Jupiter by Ptolemy and later to Neptune. The Sun dissolves into the sea: you are intuitive, compassionate and moved by music, art and other people’s pain. Boundaries are thin, so you absorb the moods around you. Bailey saw the sign of the saviour and the one that rules our present age; the French school reads dissolution, faith and the unconscious. The shadow is escape, confusion and martyrdom. The lesson: kindness needs a shore to stand on.'),
]
